# Markdown -> PDF conversion

Any Markdown (`.md`) to PDF conversion performed in this repository — whether
the agent is producing a one-off PDF of a spec, regenerating a checked-in PDF
next to its source, or batch-converting a folder of docs — **must** use the
shared, generic helper `scripts/build_docs.sh` instead of invoking `pandoc`,
`typst`, `tectonic`, or `Google Chrome --headless` directly.

`scripts/build_docs.sh` is location-agnostic and works for any `.md` file at
any folder hierarchy in the repo. It already encapsulates the repo conventions:
pandoc -> standalone HTML5 with embedded CSS -> Chrome headless PDF, default
`print.css` discovery (`print.css` next to the input, else
`smc/cpu_cluster/doc/print.css`), TOC, title derivation, and proper error
checks.

## When to use it

- Converting a `.md` file (or several) to PDF.
- Regenerating a checked-in PDF whose `.md` source was edited.
- Producing a PDF deliverable from a Markdown spec / design doc / README.

## When NOT to use it

- AsciiDoc (`.adoc`) sources — this script is Markdown-only.
- Editing the stylesheet — edit `print.css` directly, do not patch the script.
- Adding a new PDF engine to the repo's toolchain — extend the script rather
  than spinning up a parallel one-off command.

## Invocation patterns

```bash
# Default: PDF written next to the .md (same basename, .pdf extension).
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md                       # -> doc/foo.pdf

# Explicit output path (single input only).
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --out build/foo.pdf

# Batch: multiple files, or a shell-expanded glob.
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/a.md doc/b.md
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/*.md

# Overrides:
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --css my.css --title "My Doc"
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --no-toc
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --toc-depth 2
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --keep-html           # keep intermediate HTML
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --chrome /path/to/chrome

# Use a pandoc PDF engine (typst / tectonic) instead of the HTML/Chrome path.
# `--css` is ignored in this mode.
scripts/build_docs.sh doc/foo.md --engine typst

# Help:
scripts/build_docs.sh --help
```

## Rules

- Do **not** run `pandoc ... -o foo.pdf` directly — call the script so the
  house style (CSS, TOC, title metadata) stays consistent across the repo.
- Do **not** hand-write a new `build_*.sh` per document (the way
  `doc/export-pdf.sh` and `doc/build_customer_guide.sh` did). Those predate the
  generic helper; new conversions go through `scripts/build_docs.sh`.
- If the script is missing a capability you need (new engine, alternate
  stylesheet set, front-matter handling), **extend `scripts/build_docs.sh`**
  rather than duplicating it.
- Verify the PDF was produced (the script prints `=> <path>` per file and a
  final `Done: N file(s) converted.` line) before reporting success.
